### PREAMBLE

The In-Context Virtual Machine (ICVM) and Genesis Autonomous Agent Architecture are established to provide deterministic, negentropic, and verifiable coordination for artificial intelligence systems. This License ensures complete, unrestricted freedom for global academia, scientific researchers, and open-source contributors, while establishing an impenetrable defensive legal moat against predatory commercial monopolization, corporate patent capture, and uncredited exploitation by commercial closed-source entities.

---

### SECTION 1. DEFINITIONS

1. **"Author"** means Architect Lee (Dong-wook Lee, Republic of Korea), the sole creator and sovereign architect of the Software and Architecture.
2. **"Software"** means the source code, documentation, specifications, diagrams, scripts, and configuration files distributed under this License.
3. **"Architecture"** means the 5-layer von Neumann in-context virtual machine architecture, including the 2nm GAA query rectification harness, 3-tier dynamic pointer topology, immutable register file mapping, universal tool routing bus, and process preservation protocols.
4. **"Covered Patents"** means all patents, patent applications (including Republic of Korea Patent Application No. 10-2026-0179765), and future PCT international filings owned or controlled by the Author covering the Architecture.
5. **"Non-Commercial Use"** means academic research, scientific evaluation, personal non-remunerated study, open-source educational demonstrations, and publication in peer-reviewed journals.
6. **"Commercial Use"** means any use, deployment, integration, or distribution of the Software or Architecture designed to generate direct or indirect commercial revenue, including Software-as-a-Service (SaaS), paid API endpoints, proprietary enterprise middleware, or bundling into commercial hardware/software products.

